# Matlab Program: Ultrasound Signal Frequency Analysis

## Complete Program

```matlab
%% Ultrasound Signal Analysis: Time Domain to Frequency Domain
% Converts Voltage vs Time signal to Magnitude (dB) vs Frequency (MHz)
% =========================================================================

clc;
clear all;
close all;

%% ========== SECTION 1: LOAD OR GENERATE SIGNAL ==========

% --- Option A: Load real data from file ---
% data = load('ultrasound_signal.txt');  % or .csv, .mat
% time = data(:,1);      % Time column (seconds)
% voltage = data(:,2);   % Voltage column (Volts)

% --- Option B: Generate synthetic ultrasound signal (for demonstration) ---
fs = 100e6;              % Sampling frequency (100 MHz)
dt = 1/fs;              % Time step (seconds)
T  = 10e-6;             % Total signal duration (10 microseconds)
time = 0:dt:T-dt;       % Time vector (seconds)
N  = length(time);      % Number of samples

% Simulate a typical ultrasound pulse (tone burst + noise)
f0     = 5e6;           % Center frequency 5 MHz
bw     = 0.6;           % Fractional bandwidth (60%)
sigma  = 1/(pi * f0 * bw);  % Gaussian envelope width

% Gaussian-modulated sinusoidal pulse
t0      = 2e-6;         % Pulse arrival time
voltage = exp(-((time - t0).^2) / (2*sigma^2)) .* cos(2*pi*f0*(time - t0));

% Add background noise (optional, comment out if not needed)
SNR_dB  = 30;           % Signal-to-Noise Ratio in dB
noise_amp = 10^(-SNR_dB/20);
voltage = voltage + noise_amp * randn(1, N);

fprintf('Signal loaded successfully.\n');
fprintf('Sampling Frequency : %.1f MHz\n', fs/1e6);
fprintf('Number of Samples  : %d\n', N);
fprintf('Signal Duration    : %.2f µs\n', T*1e6);

%% ========== SECTION 2: PREPROCESSING ==========

% --- Apply time windowing (optional but recommended) ---
% Reduces spectral leakage
window_type = 'hanning';   % Options: 'hanning', 'hamming', 'blackman', 'none'

switch lower(window_type)
    case 'hanning'
        win = hanning(N)';
    case 'hamming'
        win = hamming(N)';
    case 'blackman'
        win = blackman(N)';
    case 'none'
        win = ones(1, N);
    otherwise
        win = hanning(N)';
end

voltage_windowed = voltage .* win;
fprintf('Window applied     : %s\n', window_type);

%% ========== SECTION 3: FFT COMPUTATION ==========

% --- Zero-padding for better frequency resolution (optional) ---
Nfft = 2^nextpow2(N) * 4;   % Next power of 2, multiplied for smoother spectrum
fprintf('FFT Points (Nfft)  : %d\n', Nfft);

% --- Perform FFT ---
Y = fft(voltage_windowed, Nfft);

% --- Compute single-sided spectrum ---
% Take only positive frequencies (first half of FFT output)
Y_single = Y(1:Nfft/2+1);

% --- Compute magnitude ---
% Normalize and scale for single-sided spectrum
magnitude = abs(Y_single) / N;       % Normalize by number of samples
magnitude(2:end-1) = 2*magnitude(2:end-1);  % Double for single-sided (except DC and Nyquist)

% --- Frequency vector (MHz) ---
freq_Hz  = (0:Nfft/2) * (fs/Nfft);  % Frequency in Hz
freq_MHz = freq_Hz / 1e6;            % Convert to MHz

%% ========== SECTION 4: CONVERT TO DECIBELS (dB) ==========

% --- Convert magnitude to dB ---
% Reference value: peak magnitude (normalized spectrum)
magnitude_dB = 20 * log10(magnitude + eps);   % eps avoids log10(0)

% --- Normalize to 0 dB peak (optional) ---
magnitude_dB_norm = magnitude_dB - max(magnitude_dB);   % Peak = 0 dB

%% ========== SECTION 5: EXTRACT KEY PARAMETERS ==========

% --- Frequency range of interest ---
f_min = 0;       % MHz
f_max = fs/(2*1e6);  % Nyquist frequency in MHz

% --- Find -6 dB bandwidth ---
peak_val = max(magnitude_dB_norm);
threshold = peak_val - 6;   % -6 dB point

[~, peak_idx] = max(magnitude_dB_norm);
center_freq = freq_MHz(peak_idx);

% Find lower -6 dB frequency
left_side = magnitude_dB_norm(1:peak_idx);
lower_idx = find(left_side >= threshold, 1, 'first');

% Find upper -6 dB frequency
right_side = magnitude_dB_norm(peak_idx:end);
upper_idx = peak_idx + find(right_side >= threshold, 1, 'last') - 1;

if ~isempty(lower_idx) && ~isempty(upper_idx)
    f_lower = freq_MHz(lower_idx);
    f_upper = freq_MHz(upper_idx);
    BW_6dB  = f_upper - f_lower;
    frac_BW = (BW_6dB / center_freq) * 100;
else
    f_lower = NaN; f_upper = NaN;
    BW_6dB  = NaN; frac_BW = NaN;
end

% --- Print Results ---
fprintf('\n========== FREQUENCY ANALYSIS RESULTS ==========\n');
fprintf('Center Frequency   : %.2f MHz\n', center_freq);
fprintf('Lower -6dB Freq    : %.2f MHz\n', f_lower);
fprintf('Upper -6dB Freq    : %.2f MHz\n', f_upper);
fprintf('-6 dB Bandwidth    : %.2f MHz\n', BW_6dB);
fprintf('Fractional BW      : %.1f %%\n', frac_BW);
fprintf('=================================================\n');

%% ========== SECTION 6: PLOTTING ==========

figure('Name','Ultrasound Signal Analysis','Color','white','Position',[100 100 1200 800]);

% --- Plot 1: Time Domain Signal ---
subplot(2,2,1);
plot(time*1e6, voltage, 'b', 'LineWidth', 1.2);
xlabel('Time (\mus)', 'FontSize', 12);
ylabel('Voltage (V)', 'FontSize', 12);
title('Time Domain Signal', 'FontSize', 13, 'FontWeight', 'bold');
grid on;
xlim([time(1)*1e6, time(end)*1e6]);
set(gca, 'FontSize', 11);

% --- Plot 2: Windowed Signal ---
subplot(2,2,2);
plot(time*1e6, voltage_windowed, 'r', 'LineWidth', 1.2);
xlabel('Time (\mus)', 'FontSize', 12);
ylabel('Voltage (V)', 'FontSize', 12);
title(['Windowed Signal (' window_type ')'], 'FontSize', 13, 'FontWeight', 'bold');
grid on;
xlim([time(1)*1e6, time(end)*1e6]);
set(gca, 'FontSize', 11);

% --- Plot 3: Frequency Spectrum (Linear) ---
subplot(2,2,3);
plot(freq_MHz, magnitude, 'g', 'LineWidth', 1.5);
xlabel('Frequency (MHz)', 'FontSize', 12);
ylabel('Magnitude', 'FontSize', 12);
title('Frequency Spectrum (Linear)', 'FontSize', 13, 'FontWeight', 'bold');
xlim([f_min, min(f_max, 2*f0/1e6 + 10)]);
grid on;
set(gca, 'FontSize', 11);

% --- Plot 4: Frequency Spectrum (dB) --- MAIN OUTPUT ---
subplot(2,2,4);
plot(freq_MHz, magnitude_dB_norm, 'k', 'LineWidth', 1.8);
hold on;

% Mark center frequency
plot(center_freq, 0, 'r*', 'MarkerSize', 12, 'DisplayName', ...
    sprintf('Center: %.2f MHz', center_freq));

% Mark -6 dB points and bandwidth
if ~isnan(BW_6dB)
    yline(-6, 'b--', '-6 dB', 'LineWidth', 1.2, 'FontSize', 10);
    plot([f_lower, f_upper], [-6, -6], 'b|-', 'LineWidth', 2, 'MarkerSize', 15);
    text(center_freq, -8, sprintf('BW = %.2f MHz', BW_6dB), ...
        'HorizontalAlignment','center', 'FontSize', 10, 'Color','blue');
end

% Mark -20 dB line
yline(-20, 'm:', '-20 dB', 'LineWidth', 1.0, 'FontSize', 9);

xlabel('Frequency (MHz)', 'FontSize', 12);
ylabel('Magnitude (dB)', 'FontSize', 12);
title('Frequency Spectrum (dB) - Main Output', 'FontSize', 13, 'FontWeight', 'bold');
xlim([f_min, min(f_max, center_freq*2.5)]);
ylim([-60, 5]);
legend(sprintf('Center: %.2f MHz', center_freq), 'Location', 'southeast', 'FontSize', 10);
grid on;
set(gca, 'FontSize', 11);

sgtitle('Ultrasound Signal: Voltage-Time to Magnitude(dB)-Frequency Conversion', ...
    'FontSize', 14, 'FontWeight', 'bold');

%% ========== SECTION 7: SAVE RESULTS ==========

% Save frequency spectrum data to CSV
output_table = table(freq_MHz', magnitude', magnitude_dB_norm', ...
    'VariableNames', {'Frequency_MHz', 'Magnitude_Linear', 'Magnitude_dB'});

% Only save up to Nyquist or a meaningful frequency
save_idx = freq_MHz <= min(f_max, center_freq * 3);
output_table = output_table(save_idx, :);

writetable(output_table, 'ultrasound_frequency_spectrum.csv');
fprintf('\nFrequency spectrum saved to: ultrasound_frequency_spectrum.csv\n');

% Save figure
saveas(gcf, 'ultrasound_analysis.png');
fprintf('Figure saved to: ultrasound_analysis.png\n');
```

---

## Key Steps Explained

| Step | Operation | Purpose |
|------|-----------|---------|
| **1** | Load/Generate signal | Voltage vs Time input |
| **2** | Apply window function | Reduce spectral leakage |
| **3** | `fft()` + normalize | Convert to frequency domain |
| **4** | `20*log10(magnitude)` | Convert to dB scale |
| **5** | Single-sided spectrum | Show 0 to Nyquist only |
| **6** | -6 dB bandwidth | Extract transducer parameters |

---

## Expected Output

```
Signal loaded successfully.
Sampling Frequency : 100.0 MHz
Number of Samples  : 1000
FFT Points (Nfft)  : 4096

========== FREQUENCY ANALYSIS RESULTS ==========
Center Frequency   : 5.00 MHz
Lower -6dB Freq    : 3.51 MHz
Upper -6dB Freq    : 6.49 MHz
-6 dB Bandwidth    : 2.98 MHz
Fractional BW      : 59.6 %
=================================================
```

> **To use with real data:** Uncomment **Option A** in Section 1, replace `'ultrasound_signal.txt'` with your filename, and adjust `fs` to your actual sampling frequency.

